WEBVTT

00:00:01.790 --> 00:00:03.000
The match is over!

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:10.040
The winner: Hawthorn Grattor!

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:17.880
Woo. You're so cool, Hawthorn.

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:55.530
Sally and a Crossroads

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:56.260
You see what I did back there?

00:01:56.760 --> 00:02:00.060
Well... It's nice that you had 
such a weak opponent.

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:03.140
Hey, hang on a minute!

00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:05.570
Well, forget it.

00:02:05.570 --> 00:02:08.520
I'm gonna win the
 Barquend Martial Arts Tournament

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:11.900
and get us a purse full of cash!

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:14.570
Well, let us know when you win!

00:02:14.570 --> 00:02:15.490
Huh?

00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:17.400
You're not even gonna watch?!

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:21.410
Are you sure we shouldn't watch him?

00:02:23.170 --> 00:02:25.780
I just don't find that stuff 
all that interesting!

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:27.410
Agreed.

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:31.420
But why did Hawthorn 
enter the tournament, anyway?

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:33.450
For the prize money, of course!

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:35.970
The grand prize is three hundred gold pieces!

00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:39.550
It's not about money. 
Gallant heart, more likely.

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:42.050
"Gallant heart"?

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:44.680
What's that?

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:46.810
Want to get strong.

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:48.270
Want to be strong.

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:49.560
Want to protect others.

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:52.310
That kind of heart.

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:56.070
Is that a thing?

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:57.240
It is.

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:01.570
The human "heart"...

00:03:02.110 --> 00:03:03.570
I find it curious.

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:10.370
When I was an ogre, I thought of humans 
as insects to be crushed.

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:13.620
I never considered 
that they might have hearts.

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:16.990
But now...

00:03:17.990 --> 00:03:20.380
You understand human hearts?

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:22.390
I'm beginning to.

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:26.350
<i>That's great to see!</i>

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:30.950
<i>It makes me think that peace with the ogres 
might be possible some day.</i>

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:36.610
<i>Mi—</i>

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:37.860
Carrot, Frau!

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:39.520
Sorry, gotta go!

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:42.970
Sorry!

00:03:47.230 --> 00:03:48.120
Mikoto!

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:54.440
I knew it was you!

00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:56.370
Sally...

00:03:56.980 --> 00:03:58.630
It's been a while, hasn't it?

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:09.610
I'm sorry.

00:04:09.610 --> 00:04:12.080
The water was all I could afford.

00:04:12.490 --> 00:04:14.020
I don't mind at all!

00:04:15.450 --> 00:04:17.770
I'm a little low on money, you see...

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:22.150
What a meal!

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:24.050
I'm stuffed!

00:04:24.050 --> 00:04:26.270
Are you, finally?

00:04:26.270 --> 00:04:27.750
I'm glad to hear it.

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:30.040
I'll be on my way, then.

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:31.280
Goodbye.

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:32.790
How come?!

00:04:32.790 --> 00:04:35.050
How can you treat me like that, you brute?!

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:37.290
"Brute"?

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:39.890
If I keep paying your dinner bill,

00:04:39.890 --> 00:04:42.300
I won't be able to afford room and board.

00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:45.690
So it's all about money, huh?

00:04:45.690 --> 00:04:47.550
Which is more important? Money or me?!

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:48.540
Money.

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:50.430
You ogre!

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:54.510
If you want to stay with me, 
you'll have to pay for your own meals.

00:04:57.190 --> 00:05:01.220
But it's not like I can just get a job...

00:05:03.430 --> 00:05:05.660
The Barquend Martial Arts Tournament...

00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:09.580
Grand prize...

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:11.570
Three hundred gold?!

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:19.690
I'm sorely low on funds at the moment,

00:05:19.690 --> 00:05:21.480
but that might change soon.

00:05:22.490 --> 00:05:24.340
Are you fighting in the tournament?

00:05:24.610 --> 00:05:27.040
You'll win it easily!

00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:30.850
I'm not. But the source 
of my money troubles is.

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:32.470
Take that!

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:34.120
Match over!

00:05:35.010 --> 00:05:36.980
Winner... Sister Millia!

00:05:38.970 --> 00:05:39.980
For real?

00:05:41.970 --> 00:05:45.000
I was trying to smash his darn face in.

00:05:47.060 --> 00:05:50.220
I'm so weak without my ogre power.

00:05:58.610 --> 00:06:00.380
I beg your forgiveness!

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:04.000
I was unable to apprehend Hatsuki.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:05.360
Oh, about that?

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:06.880
That's not your fault.

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:08.770
You had a bad match-up. 
That's all.

00:06:08.770 --> 00:06:09.800
Match-up?

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:12.340
You mean you saw it happen?

00:06:12.340 --> 00:06:13.640
Of course I did.

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:16.170
You know how I like to watch.

00:06:16.940 --> 00:06:18.520
I saw everything.

00:06:19.410 --> 00:06:24.860
Including the fact that you ran off, 
without fighting, from a single glare.

00:06:25.290 --> 00:06:26.620
I...

00:06:27.790 --> 00:06:28.780
Hey! You!

00:06:32.190 --> 00:06:34.860
Pick me up! Pick me up! Hurry!

00:06:35.270 --> 00:06:36.770
What's a child doing here?

00:06:36.770 --> 00:06:38.030
Hey, you!

00:06:38.030 --> 00:06:40.780
Show my master some respect!

00:06:40.780 --> 00:06:44.040
A mid ogre like you should know his place!

00:06:44.390 --> 00:06:46.120
Shut up, Blue!

00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:47.550
B-But...

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:48.850
So sorry.

00:06:48.850 --> 00:06:50.300
I should have handled 
the introductions earlier.

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:53.430
That creature on the ground is Somenki.

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:56.680
His maker is Kishin, beside you.

00:06:56.970 --> 00:06:58.650
The God of Masks.

00:06:58.500 --> 00:07:00.690
God of Masks 
Juselino

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:01.820
Kishin...

00:07:03.710 --> 00:07:06.520
Forgive me, my lady! 
I did not recognize you!

00:07:06.520 --> 00:07:07.900
That's okay! Just pick me up!

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:09.190
Carry me!

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:10.110
Ma'am!

00:07:23.260 --> 00:07:24.330
Is this...

00:07:26.490 --> 00:07:27.950
a summoning circle?

00:07:27.950 --> 00:07:29.210
Yep!

00:07:30.480 --> 00:07:31.970
It looks real nice.

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:34.200
Good job, Yellow!

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:34.910
Ma'am.

00:07:35.470 --> 00:07:38.000
What are they trying to use my fortress for?

00:07:40.200 --> 00:07:42.070
Just a minor gathering...

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:44.750
The Hundred Ogre Gathering.

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:47.390
The Hundred Ogre Gathering?

00:07:58.210 --> 00:08:02.210
<i>A coming together of ogres 
from across the land...</i>

00:08:03.050 --> 00:08:04.000
Your attention, please.

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:07.420
I appreciate your efforts in coming here.

00:08:08.860 --> 00:08:14.440
The 672nd Hundred Ogre Gathering 
will now begin.

00:08:17.050 --> 00:08:18.930
Now, if I may...

00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:22.940
Please have a look at this map.

00:08:26.440 --> 00:08:31.820
The red represents the sphere of influence 
of ogres on this continent.

00:08:32.440 --> 00:08:34.450
This is its current state.

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:36.690
Impossible! It can't be!

00:08:36.690 --> 00:08:39.950
But it's true. There are fewer high ogres 
gathered here than last time.

00:08:44.020 --> 00:08:46.460
Is it the work of the Peach Boy?

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:48.400
Oh?

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:50.810
Indeed it is, old master.

00:08:51.250 --> 00:08:55.240
Yes, that is one of the topics 
of this Hundred Ogre Gathering.

00:08:56.750 --> 00:08:58.360
The Peach Boy.

00:08:59.450 --> 00:09:00.460
<i>Peach Boy?</i>

00:09:01.410 --> 00:09:02.960
<i>Is that who he was?</i>

00:09:03.730 --> 00:09:06.790
Sumeragi! What is this "Peach Boy"?

00:09:06.790 --> 00:09:10.230
What forces does it command 
to drive the ogres back?

00:09:10.450 --> 00:09:12.160
Forces?

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:16.160
No, "Peach Boy" is the name 
of a single human.

00:09:18.860 --> 00:09:22.380
A single human has done 
that much damage to ogrekind?

00:09:22.380 --> 00:09:24.880
Sumeragi! What nonsense is this?

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:27.000
It's anything but nonsense.

00:09:27.340 --> 00:09:31.000
He slaughtered an army 
of ogres and killed Moki!

00:09:31.240 --> 00:09:36.190
The Peach Boy's power 
exceeds that of any army.

00:09:39.440 --> 00:09:40.520
That's right.

00:09:40.520 --> 00:09:41.920
And it wasn't just Moki.

00:09:41.920 --> 00:09:43.770
He killed Sett, as well.

00:09:43.770 --> 00:09:49.230
Juki and Kyuketsuki were 
also among his recent kills.

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:54.240
The situation is far worse 
than you're imagining.

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:57.620
If nothing is done,

00:09:58.250 --> 00:10:04.040
the Peach Boy will 
render our kind extinct.

00:10:04.280 --> 00:10:05.340
Enough!

00:10:12.490 --> 00:10:13.780
Todoroki?

00:10:13.610 --> 00:10:15.550
High Ogre 
Todoroki

00:10:15.550 --> 00:10:18.490
Sumeragi, just what are you after?

00:10:18.490 --> 00:10:20.020
What exactly do you mean?

00:10:20.550 --> 00:10:24.060
I'll grant you the existence 
of this powerful Peach Boy.

00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:27.060
But why do you stoke fear unnecessarily?

00:10:27.060 --> 00:10:31.440
Why not propose banding together to slay it?

00:10:32.090 --> 00:10:33.200
He's right!

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:35.100
If we all attack at once...

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:37.320
Silly little thing.

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:41.820
I was hoping to avoid frightening you 
more than was necessary, but...

00:10:41.820 --> 00:10:43.080
Behold.

00:10:45.390 --> 00:10:47.830
The final fate of Somenki.

00:10:48.070 --> 00:10:49.710
The God of Masks created him

00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:52.670
and gave him the power of a high ogre,

00:10:52.670 --> 00:10:54.730
yet he was beheaded in one slash.

00:10:55.840 --> 00:11:01.220
There are some opponents you can't overwhelm 
with sheer numbers, Todoroki.

00:11:01.720 --> 00:11:03.280
What does that matter?

00:11:04.210 --> 00:11:08.200
To be an ogre means to fight, 
even when you know it's hopeless.

00:11:10.770 --> 00:11:11.690
Meki...

00:11:12.730 --> 00:11:15.990
You were in love with Meki, weren't you?

00:11:17.740 --> 00:11:19.410
I'm so sorry.

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:22.740
The ogre known as Meki is gone now.

00:11:25.040 --> 00:11:26.370
What are you talking about?

00:11:26.740 --> 00:11:29.130
She was killed as well,

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:31.750
by the Peach Boy.

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:35.290
It can't be true.

00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:37.750
But it is.

00:11:37.750 --> 00:11:39.340
As a high ogre, 
she should be here.

00:11:39.340 --> 00:11:42.260
The fact that she's not 
is proof enough, isn't it?

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:49.770
I'd hoped to keep that and the 
Somenki incident quiet, you see...

00:11:49.770 --> 00:11:53.840
I'm told Meki was slain 
in a particularly cruel way.

00:11:53.840 --> 00:11:57.520
Her right eye was destroyed, 
and her horn was extracted.

00:11:57.780 --> 00:12:01.160
She was robbed of both her 
ogre power and her dignity.

00:12:01.160 --> 00:12:02.280
That's awful.

00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:03.800
He'll pay.

00:12:09.410 --> 00:12:11.040
The Peach Boy...

00:12:11.900 --> 00:12:13.430
I'll kill him.

00:12:14.660 --> 00:12:17.670
I'll avenge Meki entirely on my own.

00:12:27.370 --> 00:12:30.180
The Hundred Ogre Gathering is now over.

00:12:30.780 --> 00:12:34.890
Let's all pray for Todoroki's success!

00:12:40.070 --> 00:12:42.320
Sumeragi!

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:47.240
Come, now. You played such a valuable role 
in imparting urgency to the others.

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:48.330
You should be proud!

00:12:48.610 --> 00:12:50.730
You humiliated me!

00:12:50.730 --> 00:12:52.420
This will not stand!

00:12:52.910 --> 00:12:54.260
Blue!

00:12:54.260 --> 00:12:55.740
Master!

00:12:55.740 --> 00:12:58.350
Please repair my body at once!

00:12:59.420 --> 00:13:00.780
Sorry 'bout this.

00:13:01.330 --> 00:13:02.340
Master!

00:13:03.150 --> 00:13:04.840
Please, wait—

00:13:15.470 --> 00:13:16.850
Sumeragi!

00:13:17.310 --> 00:13:18.040
Yes?

00:13:18.610 --> 00:13:22.680
Do you wanna get along with humans 
and the Peach Boy and stuff?

00:13:23.290 --> 00:13:24.860
Yes, I do.

00:13:25.710 --> 00:13:27.320
You think it's possible?

00:13:30.300 --> 00:13:32.820
A friend of mine, long ago,

00:13:32.820 --> 00:13:35.870
loved a human and was loved in return.

00:13:36.120 --> 00:13:41.380
I believe it's not impossible, at least.

00:13:41.380 --> 00:13:43.580
Love... with a human?

00:13:44.080 --> 00:13:44.940
Love...

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:47.130
Love, eh...

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:51.160
I'm sure that word has no relevance 
to you, my dear Juselino.

00:13:51.160 --> 00:13:52.610
What was that?!

00:13:52.610 --> 00:13:53.740
Let's go, Yellow!

00:13:53.740 --> 00:13:54.460
Ma'am.

00:13:55.790 --> 00:13:58.520
Sumeragi, inform me of whatever happens.

00:14:00.110 --> 00:14:02.040
I wouldn't object to helping you.

00:14:04.690 --> 00:14:08.110
I am truly delighted, O God of Masks.

00:14:08.530 --> 00:14:10.330
Okay. See ya.

00:14:20.610 --> 00:14:21.920
Lord Sumeragi...

00:14:24.020 --> 00:14:25.780
What is it, mid ogre?

00:14:27.190 --> 00:14:28.050
Nothing.

00:14:30.480 --> 00:14:32.520
<i>I can't be sure, but...</i>

00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:36.400
<i>I don't think he's working for the benefit 
of either ogres or humans.</i>

00:14:37.010 --> 00:14:40.710
<i>I can't help but feel 
he has some other goal in mind.</i>

00:14:46.690 --> 00:14:48.040
Hey! You!

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:52.700
Pick me up!

00:14:53.770 --> 00:14:56.210
Where'd this kid come from?

00:14:56.210 --> 00:14:58.710
Come on! Pick me up!

00:14:59.940 --> 00:15:02.890
Are you lost, little miss?

00:15:02.890 --> 00:15:05.450
I'm not lost! 
I'm looking for someone!

00:15:05.450 --> 00:15:06.710
Looking for someone?

00:15:06.710 --> 00:15:09.360
Yeah! I'm looking for Sumeragi!

00:15:09.360 --> 00:15:11.050
Sumeragi?

00:15:11.050 --> 00:15:12.930
Someone named "Sumeragi"?

00:15:16.440 --> 00:15:19.160
I don't know this town very well.

00:15:19.620 --> 00:15:21.740
But I guess I've gotta help.

00:15:23.590 --> 00:15:25.310
I'll help you out.

00:15:25.310 --> 00:15:26.730
Come along now!

00:15:32.750 --> 00:15:33.990
I'm Hawthorn.

00:15:33.990 --> 00:15:35.480
What's your name, little miss?

00:15:35.480 --> 00:15:36.570
Juselino.

00:15:36.570 --> 00:15:37.870
"Juselino," eh?

00:15:38.200 --> 00:15:41.130
Yeah! God of Masks, Juselino!

00:15:41.130 --> 00:15:42.800
"God of Masks"?

00:15:42.800 --> 00:15:44.970
Yep! I'm a pretty big deal!

00:15:48.400 --> 00:15:49.480
What now?

00:15:50.570 --> 00:15:52.130
Did you just fall in love with me?

00:15:52.130 --> 00:15:53.420
Is this love?

00:15:53.420 --> 00:15:55.050
Love?!

00:15:56.410 --> 00:15:59.640
I'm honored and all, 
but I'm kind of on a journey.

00:15:59.640 --> 00:16:01.250
I'd better pass.

00:16:01.250 --> 00:16:02.640
Oh?

00:16:05.150 --> 00:16:07.630
Then can we be friends?

00:16:07.630 --> 00:16:09.430
Be my friend, right now!

00:16:10.150 --> 00:16:14.160
I give my friends anything they want!

00:16:14.160 --> 00:16:17.210
Like eternal life, or great riches!

00:16:17.630 --> 00:16:20.360
I'm such a big deal, 
I can get you whatever you want!

00:16:20.360 --> 00:16:20.900
Silly.

00:16:20.900 --> 00:16:21.520
Ow!

00:16:23.310 --> 00:16:25.170
That's not what friends do.

00:16:25.700 --> 00:16:30.170
I don't know what kind of "big deal" 
you are, and I don't care.

00:16:31.100 --> 00:16:34.680
Friendship comes from 
forming a bond of trust.

00:16:35.100 --> 00:16:37.470
You can't buy it with money or prestige.

00:16:37.470 --> 00:16:38.220
Got it?

00:16:38.850 --> 00:16:40.950
Did you just lecture me?

00:16:41.700 --> 00:16:44.690
Well, I wasn't trying to—

00:16:44.690 --> 00:16:48.240
How intriguing you are!

00:16:51.660 --> 00:16:53.050
Is something the matter?

00:16:53.050 --> 00:16:54.140
No...

00:16:54.140 --> 00:16:56.440
There you are, Juselino.

00:16:57.450 --> 00:16:59.000
Sumeragi!

00:17:00.860 --> 00:17:02.700
Silly thing.

00:17:03.080 --> 00:17:05.620
What brings you here?

00:17:05.620 --> 00:17:09.680
You said you were gonna try 
to get along with humans!

00:17:09.680 --> 00:17:11.210
So I came to see humans!

00:17:11.520 --> 00:17:12.840
I see.

00:17:14.770 --> 00:17:16.890
Did you bring her here?

00:17:16.890 --> 00:17:18.720
Yeah, she drafted me.

00:17:19.210 --> 00:17:20.540
I'm Hawthorn.

00:17:20.950 --> 00:17:22.800
Would you be Sumeragi, then?

00:17:22.800 --> 00:17:24.190
I would, indeed.

00:17:24.190 --> 00:17:26.330
I'm a pastor, as you can see.

00:17:26.750 --> 00:17:29.930
I'm Juselino's caretaker, you could say.

00:17:31.380 --> 00:17:32.980
Are you a swordsman?

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:35.060
Yeah.

00:17:35.060 --> 00:17:38.330
Will you be participating 
in the tournament today, then?

00:17:38.330 --> 00:17:39.150
Sure...

00:17:40.370 --> 00:17:42.110
Well then, Juselino,

00:17:42.110 --> 00:17:46.730
why don't you repay him by cheering him on?

00:17:46.730 --> 00:17:48.000
Cheering him on?

00:17:48.810 --> 00:17:52.000
With all your heart, 
as loud as you can.

00:17:52.380 --> 00:17:54.110
I'd like that!

00:17:54.110 --> 00:17:55.510
That would be great payback!

00:17:57.420 --> 00:17:59.010
Okay! I'll do it!

00:17:59.540 --> 00:18:01.120
Okay, I'm off then.

00:18:01.740 --> 00:18:03.530
Bye bye, Hawthorn!

00:18:04.410 --> 00:18:06.190
<i>Hawthorn Grattor...</i>

00:18:07.620 --> 00:18:11.640
<i>The regimental commander 
of the former Kingdom of Rimdarl...</i>

00:18:17.780 --> 00:18:23.160
<i>Which was, of course, destroyed by...</i>

00:18:28.800 --> 00:18:30.810
Be good to each other, won't you?

00:18:32.730 --> 00:18:33.610
Sure!

00:18:37.710 --> 00:18:38.930
Awright!

00:18:39.290 --> 00:18:41.950
I'mma get out and win more, Mikoto!

00:18:42.810 --> 00:18:44.110
I'm heading out, too.

00:18:44.910 --> 00:18:46.390
You gonna cheer me on?!

00:18:46.390 --> 00:18:49.080
No, I have somewhere else to be.

00:18:49.080 --> 00:18:51.500
Well, that just stinks!

00:18:52.380 --> 00:18:54.620
I can't cheer you on directly,

00:18:55.500 --> 00:18:58.030
but I'll be praying you don't get hurt.

00:18:58.950 --> 00:19:01.810
Well, thanks.

00:19:01.810 --> 00:19:04.200
Get yourself to the finals, won't you?

00:19:04.200 --> 00:19:06.150
Miss Three Hundred Gold.

00:19:06.150 --> 00:19:07.700
I have a name, y'know!

00:19:11.170 --> 00:19:13.440
Hawthorn Grattor, come forward!

00:19:15.840 --> 00:19:16.710
Okay!

00:19:16.940 --> 00:19:18.870
Hawthorn!

00:19:21.230 --> 00:19:24.220
I came to cheer you on!

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:27.720
I dunno what this is, 
but do your best!

00:19:28.420 --> 00:19:30.410
She really came, huh?

00:19:32.770 --> 00:19:36.230
Then, I'd better make a good showing!

00:19:36.670 --> 00:19:37.680
Begin!

00:19:40.250 --> 00:19:41.510
Whoa, it's so loud!

00:19:42.340 --> 00:19:43.680
I sympathize.

00:19:45.030 --> 00:19:48.220
I can't stand the noise, either.

00:19:51.250 --> 00:19:53.280
Who are you?

00:19:53.740 --> 00:19:55.850
A pleasure to meet you, my dear Sally.

00:19:55.850 --> 00:19:57.250
I am Sumeragi.

00:19:59.300 --> 00:20:01.260
I'm here to help.

00:20:01.600 --> 00:20:03.120
Help?

00:20:03.120 --> 00:20:06.760
Like you, I seek peace 
between humans and ogres.

00:20:06.760 --> 00:20:08.800
A future of coexistence.

00:20:10.280 --> 00:20:11.760
How do you know about that?

00:20:11.760 --> 00:20:13.160
Sumeragi!

00:20:18.270 --> 00:20:20.140
If it isn't Mikoto!

00:20:20.140 --> 00:20:21.370
How long it's been.

00:20:22.350 --> 00:20:23.780
You know each other?

00:20:23.780 --> 00:20:26.780
Get away from him, Sally. 
He's our enemy.

00:20:27.040 --> 00:20:28.350
Our enemy?

00:20:28.350 --> 00:20:29.480
He's an ogre.

00:20:30.740 --> 00:20:32.380
He's a high ogre.

00:20:32.380 --> 00:20:34.840
Likely a high-ranked one.

00:20:35.770 --> 00:20:36.790
What a relief!

00:20:37.010 --> 00:20:42.020
It all sounds so much more convincing 
coming from a monster-slayer.

00:20:43.300 --> 00:20:45.640
He's entirely right, Sally.

00:20:46.730 --> 00:20:51.760
I am indeed a high-ranked ogre 
with great power and influence.

00:20:52.790 --> 00:20:55.150
That is why I can make you a promise.

00:20:55.810 --> 00:20:59.320
If someone with your eyes and your power

00:20:59.320 --> 00:21:01.550
were to join hands with me,

00:21:01.550 --> 00:21:03.640
we'd be able to realize

00:21:03.640 --> 00:21:05.820
a future of coexistence 
between humans and ogres.

00:21:11.210 --> 00:21:12.830
Don't be absurd.

00:21:13.470 --> 00:21:16.630
I'd never let such a world exist.

00:21:16.630 --> 00:21:18.460
You expect me to swallow my hatred?

00:21:18.840 --> 00:21:22.610
I've sworn to kill every ogre in existence!

00:21:23.340 --> 00:21:25.260
I <i>have</i> to kill them!

00:21:28.670 --> 00:21:32.480
I made the same offer 
to Mikoto once, you see...

00:21:32.480 --> 00:21:34.400
He reacted exactly this way.

00:21:38.110 --> 00:21:40.860
<i>Mikoto, why are you so desperate?</i>

00:21:43.110 --> 00:21:44.140
Sally.

00:21:44.860 --> 00:21:48.200
Work with me, not with Sumeragi.

00:21:49.050 --> 00:21:51.370
Let's slaughter all the ogres.

00:21:52.120 --> 00:21:54.380
W-Wait a minute!

00:21:54.890 --> 00:21:56.350
Where is this coming from?

00:22:06.770 --> 00:22:09.160
<i>Whom should I choose?</i>

00:22:10.550 --> 00:22:13.110
<i>Whom should I abandon?</i>

00:23:45.920 --> 00:23:50.250
The Princess and the Peach

00:23:46.300 --> 00:23:48.780
Next time: "The Princess and the Peach."
